// endpoint_list_creation_models.proto — ListCreationModels: which models may a
// new workspace in this repository be created under? SIDEBAR section, beside
// CreateWorkspace.
//
// THE MODELS ARE THE LOGIN'S. A new workspace's session spends as the account
// root (the login: personal, work, ...) its worktree's path routes to, and
// what that login may run is the catalog the vendor last served a session on
// it (conversation.v1.ModelCatalog, kept by the daemon per login). This rpc
// answers that catalog for the login a create in the named repository would
// spend as, so a creation picker offers exactly those models and nothing else.
//
// THE ANSWER IS THE CREATE'S OWN CHECK. CreateWorkspace refuses a model this
// rpc would not offer (CreateWorkspaceError.model_not_in_catalog and
// .model_catalog_unknown), from the same login and the same stored catalog,
// so no client holds a copy of the list that could drift from the refusal.
//
// A READ. It records nothing and starts no session.

